<svg class="draw two-particles" viewBox="0 0 480 210" role="img" aria-labelledby="tp-title tp-desc">
  <title id="tp-title">Two lambda particles, with the force between them either a pull or a push</title>
  <desc id="tp-desc">
    Two panels, each showing two lambda particles as circles. On the left the arrows point from each
    particle towards the other and the line between them sags, so the force is a weak pull. On the
    right the arrows point away from each other and the line between them bows outwards, so the force
    is a push. Both are possible until a measurement decides. A sketch, not to scale.
  </desc>

  <text class="pane fade d1" x="130" y="58" text-anchor="middle">attraction</text>
  <text class="pane repel fade d1" x="346" y="58" text-anchor="middle">repulsion</text>
  <text class="anno fade d1" x="238" y="130" text-anchor="middle">or</text>

  <circle class="surface stroke d2" pathLength="1" cx="84" cy="126" r="26" />
  <circle class="surface stroke d2" pathLength="1" cx="176" cy="126" r="26" />
